      whyItWorks:
        "A solution works best when it tackles the **cause** of a problem and reaches **many people** at a price they can afford. Rail and BRT move large numbers of people without adding cars to the road, so they attack the cause of the go-slow. Eko Atlantic adds high-value land but not affordable homes, so it does little for the housing shortage. Bottom-up schemes succeed because residents know what they need most — but without government money they stay small.",
